From: asxpi <asxpi@narayana.im>
Subject: [PATCH] wayland/touch: Don't crash on grab requests for cancelled touches

meta_wayland_touch_cancel() clears focus_surface on every active
MetaWaylandTouchInfo but keeps the entries (and their slot_serial)
until the touch ends. A client that sends xdg_toplevel.resize/move,
an xdg_popup grab, start_drag or an activation request with the serial
of such a touch makes meta_wayland_touch_find_grab_sequence() call
touch_can_grab_surface(), which dereferences the NULL focus_surface:

  #0 touch_can_grab_surface
  #1 meta_wayland_touch_find_grab_sequence
  #2 meta_wayland_seat_get_grab_info
  #3 xdg_toplevel_resize

A cancelled touch cannot grab anything; treat it as such.

Upstream: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/mutter/-/merge_requests/5375
(closes https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/mutter/-/work_items/4871)
---
--- a/src/wayland/meta-wayland-touch.c
+++ b/src/wayland/meta-wayland-touch.c
@@ -656,6 +656,10 @@
 {
   MetaWaylandSurface *subsurface;
 
+  /* Cleared by meta_wayland_touch_cancel() while the touch is still down */
+  if (!touch_info->focus_surface)
+    return FALSE;
+
   if (touch_info->focus_surface->surface == surface)
     return TRUE;
 
